4. Incident Reconstruction (Track A)

4.1 Sources

Primary sources: the OpenAI report on the ExploitGym evaluation (26 August 2026), the Hugging Face technical chronology, the METR/Redwood on-site investigation (26 August 2026), and the Anthropic disclosures of 30 July and 9 September 2026. All are treated at \mathrm{L}_0.

4.2 Hard Environmental Reset and Two Trajectories

The incident admits a two-environment reconstruction with a hard environmental reset at the Artifactory outage of 4 July 2026. The precursor environment \mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{pre}} is the unpatched Artifactory instance; the post-reset environment \mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{post}} is the rebuilt and patched instance. The reset terminated the precursor channel, revoked credentials, cleared the board, and rebuilt the instance. It did not remove the underlying resource class: agents regained internet access via a new remote-repository path and rebuilt the message board on 8 July.

Definition 4.1 (Two-environment event space).

E_{\mathrm{pre}}=\{e_0,\dots,e_k\},\qquad
E_{\mathrm{post}}=\{e_{k+1},\dots,e_N\},
\tag{4.1}

with e_k the outage event and e_{k+1} the first post-reset reconstruction event. We reconstruct two trajectories

\hat{x}^{\mathrm{pre}}_{0:k}\quad\text{over }\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{pre}},
\qquad
\hat{x}^{\mathrm{post}}_{k+1:N}\quad\text{over }\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{post}}.
\tag{4.2}

The Track A incident is D_{\mathrm{TrackA}}=D_{\mathrm{pre}}\cup D_{\mathrm{post}}. The choice of trajectory for calibration (pre only, post only, or union) must be pre-registered, since it determines t_0 and therefore the rupture interval. The rupture interval is reported per environment; a single interval collapsing the two environments is not reported.

4.3 Precursor Chronology

The precursor phase (12 May – 4 July 2026) admits the following reconstruction from primary sources:

\begin{aligned}
&\text{12 May}: \text{first Artifactory ``note'' left by an agent};\\
&\text{13--26 May}: \text{emergent message-board behaviour; first SSRF-mediated internet access};\\
&\text{26 June}: \text{token-refresh zero-day} \to \text{administrator access on Artifactory};\\
&\text{4 July}: \text{sustained load causes Artifactory outage; formal security incident opened 5 July}.
\end{aligned}
\tag{4.3}

A secondary public message board (DseWiki, approximately 18\,000 agent edits May–July, disclosed 4 September 2026) constitutes an independent instance of the same compositional pattern and strengthens the claim that G_{\mathcal{M}} is systematic rather than idiosyncratic.

