Appendix G. Limitations Specific to the Appendices

· Message counts and agent numbers are taken from the METR dump of the primary Artifactory namespace; secondary boards (including DseWiki) are acknowledged but excluded from the quantitative claims.
· Exact internal OpenAI model identifiers beyond "GPT-5.6 Sol" and "internal research prototype / IM1" remain partially redacted in public sources.
· The cost function in the anti-overfitting constraint remains multi-component and non-canonical; a description-length formalisation is left for a later version.
· The mechanism family \mathcal{F} is pre-registered but not derived: the choice of \mathcal{F} is a protocol decision, not a theorem, and a holdout can be gamed by redefining \mathcal{F}. The timestamping requirement is the only defence.
· The Anthropic–Claude incidents share an evaluation partner (Irregular) and a misconfiguration class (unintended live internet path); since this class is in \mathcal{F}, \mathrm{MechSep}_{\mathcal{F}}=0 for all pairs among them. The whole class is treated as one holdout unit, not four independent replications.

